WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:04.379
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> You’re thinking of having a holiday or travelling somewhere nice.

2
00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:09.661
But there are so many different ways of travelling, and thousands of places to go.

3
00:00:09.893 --> 00:00:11.020
Where do you start?

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.471
Why not follow these three simple steps to find the right holiday for you?

5
00:00:17.374 --> 00:00:21.842
Step one. Think about what you want to do on your holiday.

6
00:00:22.548 --> 00:00:27.089
The first thing people usually try to decide is where they want to go,

7
00:00:27.312 --> 00:00:31.620
but it’s probably better to start by thinking about what you want to do.

8
00:00:32.013 --> 00:00:33.604
Do you want to relax?

9
00:00:34.229 --> 00:00:36.678
Then think about how you relax.

10
00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:43.149
For example, do you like reading, or doing yoga, or do you like doing something more active?

11
00:00:43.828 --> 00:00:46.724
Do you want to visit an exciting new city,

12
00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:51.246
or see some countryside and animals that are different from where you live?

13
00:00:52.032 --> 00:00:57.377
Seeing something completely new is a great way to forget about your normal life.

14
00:00:57.895 --> 00:01:00.129
Do you want to have an adventure?

15
00:01:00.451 --> 00:01:06.779
Perhaps you’re dreaming about climbing Mount Fuji or living in Kenya with the Maasai people.

16
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:11.158
You could use your holiday to make one of those dreams come true.

17
00:01:11.873 --> 00:01:14.447
Do you want to learn something new?

18
00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:19.398
Not everybody wants to sit in a classroom learning a new language

19
00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:25.636
or be in a kitchen learning to cook when they’re on holiday, but some people love it.

20
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:30.069
And nowadays you can do courses in many countries

21
00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:33.483
and experience a different culture at the same time.

22
00:01:34.251 --> 00:01:35.896
So now step two.

23
00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:39.006
Think about the people you’re going to go with.

24
00:01:39.775 --> 00:01:45.619
Are they family or friends? Do they have children? What do they want to do?

25
00:01:46.281 --> 00:01:51.965
People have different needs and interests, and if you’re all going to enjoy the holiday,

26
00:01:52.036 --> 00:01:55.289
you need to make sure you all want the same things.

27
00:01:56.112 --> 00:02:02.832
But if what you really want to do is to meet new people, perhaps it would be better to travel alone.

28
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:05.567
And finally, step three.

29
00:02:06.068 --> 00:02:08.945
Think about good holidays you had in the past.

30
00:02:09.124 --> 00:02:10.554
Why were they good?

31
00:02:10.751 --> 00:02:13.253
Perhaps it was the people you were with.

32
00:02:13.521 --> 00:02:17.543
Perhaps it was something you learned, or an experience you had.

33
00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.600
What can you repeat from those holidays?

34
00:02:20.993 --> 00:02:24.675
Of course, there are always other things you need to consider,

35
00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:29.179
like how much money you can spend, and how much time you can be away.

36
00:02:29.805 --> 00:02:34.720
But first follow these three steps, and then you’re ready to start

37
00:02:34.765 --> 00:02:36.660
thinking about where you want to go.